MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Paulo Donizeti Gardinalli Filho (@pdonizete) (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the one capability the original's provider advertises — a
web search through the MiniMax Token Plan endpoint
`POST /v1/coding_plan/search`, with the query sent as `q` (not `query`, which
the endpoint refuses as 2013 "invalid params"), the credential read in the
original's order (a key written in the section, else the variable the section
names, else `MINIMAX_CODE_PLAN_KEY`, `MINIMAX_CODING_API_KEY`,
`MINIMAX_OAUTH_TOKEN`, `MINIMAX_API_KEY`), the global and CN hosts, the
result count clamped to the endpoint's ceiling of ten, the `organic[]` rows
(title, link, snippet, date) read back in order, the in-body
`base_resp.status_code` error recognised as a failure, and a failed status
answered as text rather than an exception. What was left out: the original's
web-search-provider subclassing and its setup-panel schema, which are its
harness's registration and onboarding surfaces and have no meaning here — the
cell's section, its tool and its help topic take their place — and its
`MINIMAX_REGION` / `MINIMAX_API_HOST` environment switches, which the
section's `region` and `base_url` members state in one place instead.
